Yes, an athame is worth a wish. It provides an unlimited ammount of
E-words for fights, anytime. As opposed to wands of fire or lightning
with limited charges. Personally I spend the latter in cases where I
know that I have to fight a lot and want to be sure that the engraving
will never be erased. For most circumstances the athame is sufficient
and usable quite anytime and quite everywhere. And you can refreshen
the engraving in a single turn for more rounds of fights if necessary.

The additional +15 AC are very helpful if you have only something like
an AC:-5, but usually you have more until the mid game. If you have
already an AC:-15..-20 there's no pressing need for an additional +15.
I prefer having an athame in that case.

Wraiths? - Typically I don't need XP beyond an XL:14. Even where there
is an advantage (for example damage from a spell of magic missile) it's
sufficient effective without extreme XL. Skill slots? IME there's rarely
a need for high XL values. The HPs that you gain from XL gains? You can
get those easier with alchemy, and without the side effect of more tough
monsters to be created after XL increases.

Conflict? - Yes, that's another good option for a wish!

